    "relation": "tests",
    "tranche": "T3",
    "tranche_reason": "It compares downstream benchmark performance across parameter scales, a different measure from the held-out pretraining-loss measurements in the original scaling-law work. It does not measure cross-entropy loss or fit scaling laws.",
    "gate_note": "The paper reports average zero-shot downstream scores for linearized students at three parameter scales, which bear on V6. It does not report held-out pretraining loss, parameter/token/compute power-law fits, small-run forecasts, or compute-optimal allocations. Retrieval, instruction-adaptation, and efficiency results do not measure the claim versions being cataloged.",
    "test_reason": "The study tests V6 in a new setting: Transformer-to-subquadratic distillation. Seven student architectures show monotonically increasing average downstream scores across three parameter scales. It establishes a scale trend, without fitting or validating quantitative predictions.",
    "authors_conclusion": "The record accurately summarizes the parameter-scaling results but incompletely represents the paper's conclusion. The authors emphasize persistent architectural constraints: additional distillation through 10B tokens does not close performance gaps, and instruction adaptation does not compensate for weaker token mixers. Their suggestion of superior delta-rule scaling exponents is qualitative; no exponent estimates are reported.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "This study distills pretrained Transformer students with substituted subquadratic token mixers and evaluates average downstream-task scores. It does not use the original held-out cross-entropy scaling-law measurement or fit parameter/token/compute power laws.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Downstream scaling outcomes vary by token-mixer architecture; the ranking shifts at ∼1.7B, where Gated DeltaNet leads.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Teacher-performance recovery and architecture rankings differ at matched approximate sizes; Gated DeltaNet overtakes xLSTM at 1.7B.",
        "proposed_claim": "Token-mixer architecture affects downstream capability retained through linearization and its gains with parameter scale.",
